1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 9=

3
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:12,870
(Ada.)

4
00:01:12,870 --> 00:01:14,360
(I've shared a file.)

5
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,360
(Can you see it?)

6
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,440
Got it, Song Yang.

7
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:20,900
(Cedar headquarters management trainee
program approval, Zhou Zicheng)

8
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:26,580
(Zhou Zicheng, android development
engineer, education, work experience)

9
00:01:27,630 --> 00:01:29,040
Who's Zhou Zicheng?

10
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,550
He was an intern at Cedar Group,

11
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:33,680
working in
the AI Neural Engineering Department.

12
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:34,830
Apparently, during

13
00:01:34,830 --> 00:01:36,160
just one year at the company,

14
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,360
(Zhou Zicheng's resume)
he single-handedly solved

15
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,550
a technical problem that had troubled
the project team for years.

16
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,950
He became well known
throughout the company.

17
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:45,360
It seems Zhou Zicheng

18
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:46,830
might even be smarter than you.

19
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,360
But then again,

20
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,360
I've never seen his work myself.

21
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:52,270
Who knows if the rumors are true?

22
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,190
Okay, Song Yang.

23
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,800
Please tell me more about Zhou Zicheng.

24
00:01:59,040 --> 00:01:59,950
Anyway,

25
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,910
I just checked the records.

26
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,550
Strangely enough,

27
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:05,680
someone who seemed

28
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,910
(Zhou Zicheng's resume)
to have such a promising future

29
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:11,110
suddenly quit before becoming
a permanent employee.

30
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:14,160
Then he moved to a remote corner
of an urban village

31
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:16,390
and opened an electronics repair shop.

32
00:02:18,110 --> 00:02:19,520
Don't you think that's strange?

33
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,000
Data shows

34
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,270
that emotional factors can lead humans

35
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,360
to make life choices that are considered

36
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,240
unusual by mainstream society.

37
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,160
Such occasional cases

38
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:31,910
also fall within the normal distribution

39
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:33,190
of human diversity.

40
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:34,880
Ada.

41
00:02:35,110 --> 00:02:37,880
Right now, you just need
to say it's strange

42
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:40,040
and ask me who Zhou Zicheng is.

43
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,750
Okay, Song Yang.

44
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,800
That really is strange.

45
00:02:45,550 --> 00:02:46,750
What does Zhou Zicheng

46
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,390
have to do with

47
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:49,550
your investigation?

48
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:51,960
That's more like it.

49
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:55,520
After the incident
involving Li Senyao's double,

50
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,000
we discovered that Cedar's

51
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,080
android parts

52
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,470
were being traded on the black market.

53
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:01,910
I've spent the past few days
following the leads

54
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:03,000
and digging deeper.

55
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:04,880
I've uncovered
an underground trading network

56
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,960
far more complicated

57
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,320
than I ever imagined.

58
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,550
And Zhou Zicheng's repair shop

59
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:12,910
appears to be part of it.

60
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:14,880
(In other words,)

61
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:16,600
(his repair shop)

62
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,550
(has been secretly supplying
the black market with)

63
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:20,470
products that shouldn't
be commercially available.

64
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:23,110
Ada.

65
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:25,320
He's our next lead.

66
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:34,900
(Zhou's Warehouse)

67
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,160
(Fortune)

68
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:38,800
Ada.

69
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,110
The black market is involved in many

70
00:03:40,110 --> 00:03:41,440
illegal activities.

71
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:42,600
Don't force your way in.

72
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:44,390
Don't worry, Song Yang.

73
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,270
I'll go in pretending
to be an ordinary customer.

74
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:44,950
Hello, I'd like to repair a...

75
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,000
Normally,

76
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,160
human skin has slight
variations in conductivity.

77
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:55,600
But you

78
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,200
look more like

79
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,790
an excellent battery container.

80
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,640
What are you talking about?

81
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:16,200
Excellent craftsmanship.

82
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:19,270
Your appearance is almost
indistinguishable from a human's.

83
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:21,670
Extremely fast
emotional response processing.

84
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:25,350
Very impressive.

85
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:28,480
Could you be the latest
X-series companion android?

86
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:29,790
X21?

87
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:31,510
Oh, wait.

88
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,480
The skin texture of the 21st generation

89
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,550
isn't like this.

90
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:37,790
X22?

91
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:40,390
Sir.

92
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:42,480
I just need some technical advice

93
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:44,390
about an older module.

94
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:45,880
Sorry.

95
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,790
I can't help you.

96
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,390
A machine like you
is still under warranty.

97
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,920
I couldn't afford to repair you,

98
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,550
and it's not my place to do so.

99
00:05:53,510 --> 00:05:55,070
Tell your administrator

100
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:56,230
to contact customer support.

101
00:05:58,230 --> 00:05:59,000
Get out.

102
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:06,270
And another thing.

103
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:11,320
Stop wandering around
wearing that earpiece.

104
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:13,390
Listening in on
other people's conversations

105
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,920
(is rude.)

106
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,600
This Zhou Zicheng
really knows his stuff.

107
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:35,270
He's very unfriendly toward androids.

108
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:36,160
It's fine.

109
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:37,270
I've got another trick.

110
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:40,920
There's always a back door.

111
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:43,830
(Didn't you say not to force my way in?)

112
00:06:44,390 --> 00:06:45,160
I don't literally mean

113
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,640
climbing in through the back door.

114
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:48,760
Zhou Zicheng

115
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:50,320
has a younger brother named Zhou Zi'an.

116
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,310
I'll send you his information.

117
00:06:57,550 --> 00:06:59,760
We're going to get information
from a high school student?

118
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:01,390
Teenage boys are perfect for this.

119
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:03,200
They're naive and full
of dramatic fantasies.

120
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,600
A couple of questions
and they'll tell you everything.

121
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,830
Are you speaking
from personal experience?

122
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:06,390
Song Yang.

123
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:07,550
Of course not.

124
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,320
Anyway, there's very little information

125
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,350
about Zhou Zi'an online.

126
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:11,920
(An)
All I know is that he likes photography.

127
00:07:12,070 --> 00:07:13,640
Ada. First, find out which routes he takes

128
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:15,350
to and from school every day.

129
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,860
(An)
That might make it easier to approach him.

130
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:18,760
Zhou Zi'an.

131
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:46,180
(An)

132
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,040
Zhou Zi'an.

133
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:51,190
Help me hide, please.

134
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,480
That's strange.

135
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:54,110
Where did he go?

136
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,790
I just saw him running this way.

137
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:58,600
Zhou Zi'an.

138
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,230
Ada. There seems to be something wrong

139
00:08:06,230 --> 00:08:07,600
with your processing speed.

140
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:09,550
Who's talking?

141
00:08:09,550 --> 00:08:10,790
Are you on the phone?

142
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:13,880
It's nothing.

143
00:08:14,830 --> 00:08:16,200
She seems to have left.

144
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,830
Do we still need to stay here?

145
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:18,670
I'm so sorry.

146
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:19,480
Sorry.

147
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,600
I didn't mean to.

148
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,920
I took some photos of Ms. Ma

149
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,200
physically punishing students.

150
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,200
She caught me,

151
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:25,390
so she's been chasing me.

152
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:27,790
But you could've just
hidden on your own.

153
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,790
I could've covered for you.

154
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:31,110
You're right.

155
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:32,790
I'm really sorry.

156
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,230
I was so panicked just now.

157
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:35,880
I...

158
00:08:36,710 --> 00:08:38,790
Let me buy you some milk tea
to make up for it.

159
00:08:39,590 --> 00:08:40,230
By the way,

160
00:08:40,470 --> 00:08:41,440
are you a student, too?

161
00:08:41,590 --> 00:08:42,320
Or...

162
00:08:46,550 --> 00:08:48,080
I graduated from First High School.

163
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,790
I'm now studying photography
at Hua University.

164
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,150
I came back to my old school

165
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,030
to organize a photography exhibition.

166
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,550
So you're a senior.

167
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:56,640
I want to study photography
at Hua University, too.

168
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:57,710
Senior,

169
00:08:57,790 --> 00:08:59,440
I'm definitely buying you that milk tea.

170
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,520
Your photos are really good.

171
00:09:14,670 --> 00:09:15,520
Not at all.

172
00:09:15,710 --> 00:09:17,470
I'm sure you have much more
experience than I do.

173
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:21,550
Senior.

174
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,030
(You've finally remembered
your mission.)

175
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:49,150
You forgot that the earpiece
is just for show.

176
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:51,080
During missions,

177
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,960
your auditory module
is connected to mine.

178
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:54,030
I know.

179
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:56,200
I just didn't want Zhou Zi'an
to get suspicious.

180
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,080
There seems to be

181
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,400
a natural connection between us.

182
00:10:03,150 --> 00:10:05,520
(I believe humans would call
this feeling)

183
00:10:06,590 --> 00:10:07,590
friendship.

184
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,670
I think he's my first friend.

185
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,790
You think Zhou Zi'an

186
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:16,200
is your first friend?

187
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,200
(Song Yang.)

188
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,790
(You seem to have something to say.)

189
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:21,230
It's nothing.

190
00:10:21,470 --> 00:10:22,400
(Anyway,)

191
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,400
(it looks like you've gained)

192
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,590
(Zhou Zi'an's trust now.)

193
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:25,960
(What's the next step?)

194
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:27,790
I promised to bring him some information

195
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:29,200
about Hua University's
photography program tomorrow.

196
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,790
(I'll need your help with that.)

197
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,840
I'll go see him again tomorrow

198
00:10:33,350 --> 00:10:34,670
and see if I can learn more

199
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:36,000
about his brother.

200
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,400
Ada.

201
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:39,520
You must be

202
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:41,080
the best android at lying.

203
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,400
From a semantic perspective,

204
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:46,150
your words suggest

205
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,400
some feelings of dissatisfaction.

206
00:10:51,470 --> 00:10:52,960
I'll go find the photography
program materials.

207
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:53,710
Over.

208
00:11:01,710 --> 00:11:02,470
Zicheng.

209
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,350
Zicheng.

210
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,200
Where have you been?

211
00:11:21,350 --> 00:11:22,590
Why are you home so late?

212
00:11:24,110 --> 00:11:24,790
I...

213
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,000
You got home

214
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,400
exactly 48 minutes later than usual.

215
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,350
Did you know that?

216
00:11:31,710 --> 00:11:32,650
Zi'an.

217
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:36,590
Never

218
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:40,400
lie to me.

219
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:43,640
Understand?

220
00:11:58,550 --> 00:11:59,760
Because

221
00:12:01,550 --> 00:12:03,400
I have to protect my little brother.

222
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:27,180
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

223
00:12:28,010 --> 00:12:32,880
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

224
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:35,790
♪That's me, too♪

225
00:12:37,330 --> 00:12:40,850
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

226
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:45,150
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

227
00:12:45,770 --> 00:12:49,560
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

228
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:52,410
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

229
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:57,010
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

230
00:12:57,010 --> 00:12:59,140
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

231
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:02,310
♪Bring me something more?♪

232
00:13:03,010 --> 00:13:09,740
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

233
00:13:10,570 --> 00:13:13,970
♪Sadness is blue♪

234
00:13:14,950 --> 00:13:18,190
♪How would you paint me?♪

235
00:13:19,190 --> 00:13:22,920
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

236
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:25,180
♪Painting without restraint♪

237
00:13:25,370 --> 00:13:27,960
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

238
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:32,150
♪If I could start over♪

239
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:36,220
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

240
00:13:36,330 --> 00:13:38,970
♪Give me back my smile♪

241
00:13:39,570 --> 00:13:42,050
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

242
00:13:42,550 --> 00:13:47,790
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪
